cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SafeTune in research, please cite the paper below."
title: "SafeTune: A Unified, Faithful Library for Auditing and Repairing Safety Drift in Fine-Tuned LLMs"
abstract: >-
  SafeTune is a source-available library that unifies drift-induction,
  repair, and evaluation for safety alignment in fine-tuned LLMs. It hosts
  four repair paradigms (weight patching, safety-constrained retraining,
  gradient-based unlearning, inference-time steering), with implementations
  audited against their originating papers, plus interpretability and
  evaluation instrumentation.
